CHANGES MADE TO GTS
---------------------
06/06/07  Moved the reading and broadcasting of the input parameters from
          INPUT.d into a subroutine. That subroutine is in setup_v2.F90.

06/06/07  Created a module called "mpi_defs" to be used whenever MPI calls
          are needed in a subroutine or function. This allows us to only
          "use" only a few definitions from mpif.h instead of loading the whole
          include file every time. For example, the module "precision" contains
          the statement "use mpi_defs,only:MPI_DOUBLE_PRECISION,MPI_REAL".

06/06/07  In C function "esiread()" called in setup, which reads the
          equilibrium file, added code to have only the root process (mype=0)
          read the file and then broadcast the quantities just read to the
          other processes.

06/13/07  In subroutines "read_profiles" and "read_profiles_NSTX" (found in
          spl_profile.F90), made the root process read the data files and
          broadcast values to the other processes.

06/13/07  In smooth, used pre-processor statements to choose the type of FFT
          routine to be called. If __ESSL is defined, the ESSL FFT routine is
          called directly. If not, we use the fftr1d interface.

06/13/07  Added the file "fft_gl.f90" to the distribution as a portable FFT
          routine that can be used and compiled on all platforms. It does not
          require a power-of-two number of elements and it is usually faster
          than the NAG FFT routine. (rev 61)

06/13/07  Removed the arguments to the Er_provider subroutine and moved them
          to the module "global_parameter" because they are also used in the
          new subroutine that reads and broadcasts the input parameters to the
          other processors (see setup.F90).

07/02/07  In snapshot, replaced "numberpe" by "ntoroidal" in loop that writes
          out "eachpsi" to file.

07/03/07  In diagnosis, in sending the tracer information to the root process
          at the beginning of the routine, the MPI_SEND is called only if the
          tracer information is not on the root process already. There was an
          error in the if statement. I replaced  "if(mype==0)call MPI_SEND"
          by "if(mype/=0)call MPI_SEND". (rev 62)

07/03/07  In smooth, replaced the numerical factor "1.0" passed as an argument
          to the fftr1d routine by the variable "scale" to handle single to
          double precision issues. (rev 63)

07/05/07  Replaced implicit loop:
             enion(:)=0.5*(zion(4,:)*BB(:))**2+zion(6,:)**2*BB(:)
          by an explicit loop from 1 to mi since BB() is valid for BB(1:mi) and 
          undefined for BB(mi+1:mimax), where mimax is the last dimension of
          all the particle arrays.

07/06/07  There was a typo in the following statement:
             rfac=dT_da(r,0,0)/temperature(r,0.0) 
          The function dT_da() has only 2 arguments, not 3. The argument list
          (r,0,0) should be (r,0.0).

08/16/07  I had forgotten to change "mype" to "myrank_toroidal" and "numberpe"
          to "ntoroidal" in a section of the field subroutine (field.f90).
          Do "svn diff -r 94 field.f90" to see the difference.

08/17/07  In the subroutine setup (setup_v2.F90), the calculation for the
          quantity describing the density of particles per cell "markeri"
          was using the wrong number of particles. It was using "mi" when
          it should have used "mi*npartdom" to have the total number of
          particles in each cell due to the particle decomposition.
          markeri(k,ij)=real(mi*npartdom)*markeri(k,ij)/eachv

11/06/07  The variable "misum" was changed to a floating point quantity to
          allow for values larger than 2 billion. "misum" is the total number
          of particles in the simulation and can easily be too large to fit
          in a 4-byte integer variable. Since it was always converted to a
          floating point number before being used in load, it was changed
          to a real value (real(wp) misum). Several 8-byte integer quantities
          are now used in load to calculate "misum" and related quantities
          (such as markeri and pmarki).

01/04/08  Revision 180 is the version of the code prior to the inclusion of
          the PETSc solver and the electron dynamics.

